WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
I have a story for you that unfortunately

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.280
you won't understand unless you understand something about Kurds.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.800
I mentioned earlier in the show that Donald Trump yesterday had one of the strangest

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.020
press conference that I've ever seen.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.380
And I was watching it, initially as I was working on a bunch of other stuff for the show,

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:23.060
And at a certain point I just had to stop focus exclusively on the press conference

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:28.060
because it was so insane. And at a certain point during this press conference Donald Trump takes a question

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:33.360
from a Kurdish journalist named Rahim Rashidi, who works for Kurdistan TV.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:40.060
And Trump calls on the guy as "Mr. Kurd", ok? Now this might not be immediately

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.420
jarring to you - although I know that to many people in the audience it will be - what you have

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.480
to understand to really understand the context here is that Kurds are an ethnic group, right

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:57.440
so "Kurd" is interchangeable in terms of like a category item with something like "black"

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.180
or "Jewish"  for example.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:06.400
So when Trump calls on someone by saying "Mr. Kurd" it's the same as if a black journalist

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.240
stood up and raised their hand and Trump says "Go ahead Mr. Black"

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.000
or a Jewish journalist stands up and [Trump] says "Next question Mr. Jew".

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.240
That is the equivalent of what Donald Trump is doing in this.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.960
Check out this very very short but extraordinarily bizarre video.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.040
TRUMP: Yes please, Mr. Kurd

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.080
*Crowd murmurs with some laughter*

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:30.240
TRUMP: Go ahead.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.180
JOURNALIST: Thank you very much for your time Mr. President

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:39.920
This is the sort of intangible debasement of the culture around the office of the presidency

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.820
that goes well beyond policy. It doesn't have to do with Trump's misunderstanding of trade deals

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.520
and his destructive tax plans and his  complete lack of knowledge of how money works;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:56.540
this is kind of like the flavour and character of this administration's effect making of the United States

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:03.100
just look really stupid around the world. And the problem is that Trump and his followers are too ignorant to realise

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:08.640
how sort of mindblowingly horrible this is. People will write to me - you know they will Pat - and they'll say

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.020
"David you're too sensitive it was a term of endearment" or something like that.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.860
You would only think that if you both have: number one no idea what Kurdish means,

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:24.080
and number two no understanding that this is the same as Trump calling on other reporters

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.980
by their race or ethnicity. And going back to my example where I said this would be like saying to a black reporter

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:36.480
"Next question black guy". Imagine for a second if Barack Obama during one of these press conference

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.860
- just like really think about it ok? - Obama goes up there maybe he's just had some kind of fancy mustard

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.020
maybe he's wearing a tanned suit, so people are already enraged about what he's doing,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.320
and he calls on a reporter by saying "Mr. white guy, next question please".

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.920
Trump did almost exactly that here.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.240
PAT:  Yeah and of course I don't think Trump would say "Go ahead Mr. black guy"

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.660
DAVID: Of course not.
PAT: or "Go ahead Mr. Jew".

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.720
But he doesn't understand like the historical context and why you can't say that.
DAVID: He doesn't get that it's the same thing.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:14.380
Right exactly, he doesn't realise that Kurd as a characteristic is equivalent to

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.900
someone who is ethnically Jewish or someone who's black.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.160
And by the way Trump has a moment of almost the doing exact same thing but with a black guy.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.900
Remember this absolutely ludicrous moment from a Trump presidential rally during the campaign?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.900
TRUMP: We had a case where we had an African American guy who was a fan of mine

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:33.700
DAVID: Shocking.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.700
TRUMP: Great fan. Great guy! In fact I wanna find out what's going on with him.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.240
You know what - Oh! Look at my African American over here, look at him.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.120
*David chuckles*

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.600
Are you the greatest? You know what I'm talking about? Ok.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:51.180
So we have an African American guy at one of the rallies a month ago. And he's sitting there behaving.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.360
*David laughs*

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.560
And we had protestors inside the arena.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.840
DAVID: This is like, Trump doing an impression doing an impression of the Trump

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.680
of the Trump you would expect to see on Saturday Night Live, right.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:04.440
And I was thinking as I watched the clip this morning preparing for the story,

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:10.260
we're almost like numb to this, right. Like if it had even been George W. Bush who had faux pa

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:14.780
after faux pa, and horrible display of ignorance after horrible and embarrassing display of ignorance,

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.140
time after time after time as president.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:22.800
If it was even Bush we would be reacting more strongly. But this is politics under Trump.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:29.060
"Mr. Kurd go ahead", "There's my African American", there was a black guy who was behaving at a rally, go figure.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.840
PAT: This is the kind of thing that your slightly racist Uncle says at a dinner party,

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:33.480
DAVID: Yes.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.820
PAT: and you family's all kind of used to it and you kind of give him the pass. But we shouldn't give

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.620
the same pass to the President of the United States.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:46.040
DAVID: In the same way that we shouldn't give the - it's all about context and that's why you know

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:50.680
with the Brett Kavanaugh stuff, not to go back to it I feel like we've covered it enough, it's not just

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:56.600
can this person be - I don't even want to insult anybody's job - but it's not can this be some low level

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.740
entry level thing - uh - job somewhere.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:04.640
This is the an appointment for live to the highest court in the land, it's one of the positions of greatest power

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:10.960
and responsibility in the United States period, right. And the expectation should be higher.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.300
The idea that "you know listen... it's like yeah there's multiple accusers but it was a while ago

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:21.100
and we kinda have a schedule to get to here and we wanna have the vote on Friday", we would be reacting

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:26.440
way more strongly to what Trump is doing if we weren't completely desensitised to it.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:31.800
We would be, hopefully, reacting way more strongly - or many of us are reacting strongly but others are not -

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:38.540
to the allegations against Brett Kavanaugh if we hadn't elected a president who had 16 allegations against him!

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:44.860
Right so this is all - these are horrible horrible realities that we're dealing with, but you can just tell

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.080
that so much of the population has become numb to this stuff and that's really disturbing.

